  "preamble": "The development of [a] into the rising back diphthong [uo] involves rounding, raising of the onset and diphthongization. Its textbook case is the Proto-Samic vowel shift, in which Pre-Samic first-syllable *a was lengthened, raised to *ō and broken into *uo, so that Proto-Uralic *kala 'fish' (Finnish kala) became Proto-Samic *kuolē, Northern Sami guolli.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Backing, Rounding, Diphthongization, Chain Shift",
  "languageExamples": [
    {
      "language": "Proto-Samic (from Proto-Uralic)",
      "languageFamily": "Samic",
      "examples": [
        {
          "from": "Proto-Uralic *kala 'fish'",
          "to": "Proto-Samic *kuolē > Northern Sami guolli",
          "note": "Reconstructed stage. Part of the Proto-Samic vowel shift: Pre-Samic *a was lengthened to *ā, raised to *ō and finally diphthongized to *uo in the first syllable; Finnish kala keeps the old vowel."
        },
        {
          "from": "Proto-Uralic *pala- 'to burn'",
          "to": "Proto-Samic *puolē- > Northern Sami buollit",
          "note": "Reconstructed stage; compare Finnish pala-."
        },
        {
          "from": "Proto-Uralic *taka 'back, rear'",
          "to": "Proto-Samic *tuokē > Northern Sami duohki",
          "note": "Reconstructed stage; compare Finnish taka- 'back'."
        },
        {
          "from": "Proto-Uralic *kanta- 'to carry'",
          "to": "Proto-Samic *kuontē- > Northern Sami guoddit",
          "note": "Reconstructed stage; compare Finnish kanta-."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
